  "worked_solution": "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arccos}\u2061(\\frac{2}{7})=1.281\\,044\u2026\u22481.2810\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $1.2810$ lies inside the specified domain, our first solution, rounded to one decimal place, is $x=1.3.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the first quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}=1.2810.$ Since $\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x>0,$ the second solution must lie in the fourth quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}=1.2810.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13952163/assets/1b1b50c4d13ebae81a4c8af45ec2c9fde8dc6810da78bd21f74ebcdd117a375e.png)\n\nSince the second solution $x$ lies in the $4$th quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =2\\pi -{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & =2\\pi -1.2810 \\\\  & \u22485.0022 \\\\  & \u22485.0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, arranged in ascending order, the solutions are $x=1.3$ and $x=5.0.$",
